@prefix ldh:    <https://w3id.org/atomgraph/linkeddatahub#> .
@prefix rdf:    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix dh:     <https://www.w3.org/ns/ldt/document-hierarchy#> .
@prefix dct:    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<> a dh:Item ;
    dct:title "Access control" ;
    dct:description "Agents, groups, and authorizations" ;
    rdf:_1 <#content> .

<#content> a ldh:XHTML ;
    rdf:value """<div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <p class="lead">Agents, groups, and authorizations</p>
    <p>LinkedDataHub access control is based on the W3C <a href="https://www.w3.org/wiki/WebAccessControl" target="_blank">ACL ontology</a>.</p>
    <div>
        <h2 id="access-modes">Access modes</h2>
        <p>There are four access modes (classes of operation) that map to <a href="../../http-api/">HTTP methods</a>:</p>
        <table class="table table-striped">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Mode</th>
                    <th>Permits</th>
                    <th>HTTP method</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <th>Read</th>
                    <td>Read the contents, including querying them.</td>
                    <td><code>GET</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th>Write</th>
                    <td>Overwrite the contents, including deleting or modifying them.</td>
                    <td><code>PUT</code>, <code>PATCH</code>, <code>DELETE</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th>Append</th>
                    <td>Add information without removing or replacing any.</td>
                    <td><code>POST</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th>Control</th>
                    <td>Change the authorizations that apply to the resource.</td>
                    <td>— (no corresponding HTTP method)</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="agents">Agents</h2>
        <p>An agent is a person or a piece of software, identified by a WebID, that can be authorized to have certain <a href="#access-modes">modes
            of access</a> to certain applications.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="groups">Groups</h2>
        <p>A group is a named group of <a href="#agents">agents</a> to which an <a href="#authorizations">authorization</a> can
            be given. It is a subclass of the <a href="http://xmlns.com/foaf/spec/#term_Group" target="_blank"><code>foaf:Group</code></a>
            class.</p>
        <p>There are several default groups:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Owners</li>
            <li>Writers</li>
            <li>Readers</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="alert alert-info">
            <p>By default, only members of the owners group have access to the administration application: its built-in
                <samp>Full control</samp> authorization grants the <a href="#access-modes">Control</a> mode (along with read and write)
                to that group. See <a href="#authorizations">Authorizations</a>.</p>
            <p>Note that an agent being a member of one of the above groups does not automatically provide it with an
                authorization. A valid authorization for the whole group has to be present.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="authorizations">Authorizations</h2>
        <p>An authorization explicitly grants access for an <a href="#agents">agent</a> or a <a href="#groups">group</a>
            of agents to access a specific end-user application document or a <a href="../ontologies/#classes">class</a>
            of its documents.</p>
        <p>An <a href="#agents">agent</a> has to be authorized using the <a href="#access-modes">Control</a> mode to be
            able to log in to the <a href="../../dataspace/#admin-apps">administration application</a>. By default such an
            authorization is granted to the <a href="#groups">owners group</a>.</p>
        <p>The default authorizations for groups and their respective access modes:</p>
        <table class="table table-striped">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Group</th>
                    <th>Read access</th>
                    <th>Write/append access</th>
                    <th>Full control</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <th rowspan="2">Owners</th>
                    <td rowspan="2"><a href="#access-modes">Read</a></td>
                    <td><a href="#access-modes">Write</a></td>
                    <td rowspan="2"><a href="#access-modes">Control</a></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><a href="#access-modes">Append</a></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th rowspan="2">Writers</th>
                    <td rowspan="2"><a href="#access-modes">Read</a></td>
                    <td><a href="#access-modes">Write</a></td>
                    <td rowspan="2">—</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><a href="#access-modes">Append</a></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th>Readers</th>
                    <td><a href="#access-modes">Read</a></td>
                    <td>—</td>
                    <td>—</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>An authorization is a plain RDF resource. Granting the <samp>writers</samp> group full access to the Northwind orders container:</p>
        <div class="ldhc-tabs or-horizontal">
            <div class="ldhc-tablist sz-md va-line" role="tablist">
                <button aria-controls="rdf-pane" aria-selected="true" class="ldhc-tab is-on" id="rdf-tab" role="tab" type="button"><span class="ldhc-tab-lbl">RDF</span></button>
                <button aria-controls="command-line-interface-pane" aria-selected="false" class="ldhc-tab" id="command-line-interface-tab" role="tab" type="button"><span class="ldhc-tab-lbl">Command line interface</span></button>
            </div>
            <div aria-labelledby="rdf-tab" class="ldhc-tabpanel" id="rdf-pane" role="tabpanel">
                <pre>@prefix acl:  &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#&gt; .
@prefix rdfs: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#&gt; .

&lt;#this&gt; a acl:Authorization ;
    rdfs:label "Order management" ;
    acl:agentGroup &lt;https://admin.localhost:4443/acl/groups/writers/#this&gt; ;
    acl:mode acl:Read, acl:Append, acl:Write ;
    acl:accessTo &lt;https://localhost:4443/orders/&gt; .</pre>
            </div>
            <div aria-labelledby="command-line-interface-tab" class="ldhc-tabpanel" hidden="hidden" id="command-line-interface-pane" role="tabpanel">
                <pre>ldh admin acl create-authorization \\
  --label "Order management" \\
  --agent-group "https://admin.localhost:4443/acl/groups/writers/#this" \\
  --to "https://localhost:4443/orders/" \\
  --read --append --write</pre>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p>An authorization can also target a whole class of documents with <code>acl:accessToClass</code>. Granting the <samp>readers</samp> group read access to every container:</p>
        <pre>@prefix acl:  &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#&gt; .
@prefix rdfs: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#&gt; .
@prefix dh:   &lt;https://www.w3.org/ns/ldt/document-hierarchy#&gt; .

&lt;#this&gt; a acl:Authorization ;
    rdfs:label "Container read access" ;
    acl:agentGroup &lt;https://admin.localhost:4443/acl/groups/readers/#this&gt; ;
    acl:mode acl:Read ;
    acl:accessToClass dh:Container .</pre>
        <p>A public-access authorization allows access for non-authenticated agents — the <a href="../../../tutorial/publish/">Publish</a> stage of the
            tutorial shows the one <samp>ldh admin acl make-public</samp> creates, granting <code>acl:Read</code> to the <code>foaf:Agent</code> class
            on every document class.</p>
        <div class="alert alert-info">
            <p>The owner's and <a href="../../dataspace/#dataspaces">secretary's</a> authorizations are stored under stable URIs (<samp>acl/authorizations/owner-webid/</samp> and <samp>acl/authorizations/secretary-webid/</samp>), so reloading the admin dataset does not create duplicates.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <h3 id="auth-requests">Access requests</h3>
            <p>If access is denied due to missing authorization, the agent can ask for it by issuing a request to the application's
                <a href="#groups">owners</a>. The request indicates the request URI and access mode in question.
                The owners can then accept the request by creating an <a href="#authorizations">authorization</a> with the provided information
                (possibly extending the requested access to a <a href="#groups">group</a> of agents or a <a href="../ontologies/#classes">class of resources</a>),
                or simply ignore it.</p>
            <p>A request is data too — asking for write access to a Northwind order:</p>
            <pre>@prefix lacl: &lt;https://w3id.org/atomgraph/linkeddatahub/admin/acl#&gt; .
@prefix acl:  &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#&gt; .

&lt;#this&gt; a lacl:AuthorizationRequest ;
    lacl:requestAgent &lt;https://localhost:4443/agents/jane/#this&gt; ;
    lacl:requestMode acl:Write ;
    lacl:requestAccessTo &lt;https://localhost:4443/orders/10248/&gt; .</pre>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="management">Management</h2>
        <div>
            <h3 id="management-cli"><a href="../../command-line-interface/">Command line interface</a></h3>
            <table class="table table-striped">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Action</th>
                        <th>CLI command</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Create group</th>
                        <td><a href="../../command-line-interface/#commands"><samp>ldh admin acl create-group</samp></a></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Create authorization</th>
                        <td><a href="../../command-line-interface/#commands"><samp>ldh admin acl create-authorization</samp></a></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Add agent to group</th>
                        <td><a href="../../command-line-interface/#commands"><samp>ldh admin acl add-agent-to-group</samp></a></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Make a document public</th>
                        <td><a href="../../command-line-interface/#commands"><samp>ldh admin acl make-public</samp></a></td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="lead">To request access to someone else's dataspace, see the <a href="../../../get-started/request-access/">Request access</a> guide. To open your data to the public, follow the <a href="../../../tutorial/publish/">Publish</a> stage of the tutorial.</p>
</div>"""^^rdf:XMLLiteral .